From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:12:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 116/151] Markdown typing helpers: lists, links, code,
 strikethrough, headings

In Markdown files:
- Ctrl+Shift+X strikethrough, Ctrl+` inline code (longer fence around
  backticks), Ctrl+K link from the selection or the word at the cursor,
  pasting a URL over a selection makes a link
- Ctrl+Shift+1..6 headings, Ctrl+Shift+0 plain text
- Enter continues list items, tasks and quotes; Enter on an empty item
  ends or outdents it; ordered lists renumber
- Tab / Shift+Tab nest and un-nest items with their children
- Ctrl+Enter ticks or unticks tasks
- Edit menu entries with a Heading submenu; shortcut hints in the "/" menu
- __bold__ and _italic_ are recognised when removing, also across lines
- Code blocks and front matter are left alone (lists: HTML blocks too)

